<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Thopia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1388</span> · Also known as Charles Thopia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Thopia was an Albanian nobleman who held lands in central Albania between the Mat and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkumbin">Shkumbin</a> rivers in the 14th century. Claiming Angevin descent through his mother, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> from the Angevins in 1368 and styled himself Prince of Albania. His principality was among the strongest Albanian lordships until his death in 1388, after which Durrës passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-thopia.jpg" alt="Karl Thopia" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PrekCali · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_Thopia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
